Provenance of reused or referenced material
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. yuzono/anime-extensions (https://github.com/yuzono/anime-extensions)
   Apache License 2.0.
   The repository layout (src/<lang>/<name>, lib/, lib-multisrc/, core), the Gradle convention
   plugin approach in gradle/build-logic, the extension manifest placeholders, the APK naming
   scheme and the keep-rule generation task follow the design of that repository. The code in
   this repository was written independently; no source files were copied, except that the
   LICENSE file is the standard Apache License 2.0 text.

2. komikku-app/aniyomi-extensions-lib (https://github.com/komikku-app/aniyomi-extensions-lib)
   Apache License 2.0.
   Compile-only API stubs. Not redistributed: the host app provides the implementation at
   runtime.

3. komikku-app/aniyomi-extensions-inspector
   (https://github.com/komikku-app/aniyomi-extensions-inspector)
   Mozilla Public License 2.0.
   Built from a pinned commit and executed in CI to read source metadata from APKs. Not
   redistributed and not linked into any artifact.

4. Internet Archive API responses
   (src/all/internetarchive/test/resources/fixtures/)
   Item metadata recorded from https://archive.org public APIs on 2026-10-20, trimmed and
   stripped of uploader e-mail addresses and server details. Each item's rights are stated in
   its own metadata. No media files are included. Use of the API is subject to the Internet
   Archive Terms of Use (https://archive.org/about/terms.php).

5. Launcher icon (core/src/main/res/mipmap-*)
   Generated by tools/make_icon.py; original work of this project, no third-party marks.

Runtime libraries (OkHttp, Jsoup, kotlinx.serialization, kotlinx.coroutines) are provided by the
host app and are only compile-time dependencies of this repository.
